			},
			"description": "Field Viewer - example effect: shows the Motion Bridge field texture as it arrives in a patch and measures the bridge contract. In Arena, load the Spout source 'Motion Bridge' as a clip at its own size, set the layer's Auto Size to Stretch, and put this patch on the clip (after its Transform). The panel shows: IN = size of the texture the patch gets, OUT = render size (equal = the field is stretched over the frame); BAND = where the status band was found (TOP = as the contract says, BOTTOM = rows flipped, NONE = no live band); FPS = counter steps per second, i.e. bridge frames that reach the patch (the bridge sends 30); AGE MS = milliseconds since the last change (green below 250); COUNT = the counter. The band gets a line at its inner edge and the counter as a bar. Channel: All shows red = occupancy, green = motion, blue = visibility; or one channel as grey. Show Info switches the panel and the band marks off. Shader: Resource/FieldViewer.fs.",
			"displayName": "Field Viewer",
			"identifier": "e4e85327-fd0d-43d5-9327-837b536cd094",
			"licenseName": "Unlicense",
			"mail": "S.Mazur@cati-co.de",
